     "title": "World Bolognese Ragù Day",
     "source": "Checkiday",
     "url": "https://www.checkiday.com/1d83bbd9ba1c98952d9b58d2c3ab95cf/world-bolognese-ragu-day",
     "gn_url": null,
     "desc": "World Bolognese Ragù Day was created \"to promote the ancient and authentic Italian recipe in the world.\" The first observance was held at Villa Ranuzzi Cospi, near Bologna, in the Bagnarola area of Budrio in Italy. Dishes were prepared throughout the day using Bolognese sauce. Ragù is a meat-based  Ragù is a meat-based sauce. The name is an Italian word coming from the French word ragoût , from the verb ragoûter , meaning \"to revive the taste.\" The earliest documentation of ragù served with pasta dates to the late eighteenth century in Imola , in the Metropolitan City of Bologna , the capital of Emilia-Romagna in Italy. A ragù is usually made by adding meat to soffritto , a mixture of finely chopped celery, onions, carrots, and garlic with fresh herbs. The soffritto is partially cooked in olive oil , then simmered for a long while in tomato sauce, usually with other ingredients like tomato paste, white wine , and milk, until it is a thick sauce. The specific kind of ragù celebrated today is ragù alla bolognese or ragù bolognese , called Bolognese sauce in the United States, or simply ragù in Bologna. It is the traditional ragù of Italy. Along with the ingredients mentioned above, i",
