     "id": "Hf04a39",
     "col": "humor",
     "title": "National Pumpkin Cheesecake Day",
     "source": "Checkiday",
     "url": "https://www.checkiday.com/a249613c65b32b0466a66b8a2d270366/national-pumpkin-cheesecake-day",
     "gn_url": null,
     "desc": "National Pumpkin Cheesecake Day celebrates the autumn dessert that combines creamy cheesecake with pumpkin and warm fall spices. Pumpkin cheesecake is commonly made with a graham cracker crust and a pumpkin-purée cheesecake filling, with variations that include whipped cream, caramel, pecans, or di Cheesecake itself has recorded roots in ancient Greece, but the origin of the pumpkin-cheesecake combination is unclear. Jamie Geller notes both the dessert’s ancient history and the uncertainty surrounding its pumpkin variation . The holiday’s founder and precise origins are likewise not documented. October 21 nevertheless offers a seasonal excuse to enjoy this rich dessert as fall baking gets underway. Celebrate by enjoying a slice of pumpkin cheesecake, baking one at home, or picking one up from a local bakery. Try a graham cracker or gingersnap crust, experiment with toppings such as whipped cream or pecans, and share an extra slice with friends, family, or coworkers. You can also make individual mini cheesecakes for easy sharing.",
     "outlets": 1,
     "also": [],
